    {
      "id": "claim_6ffb72fc9ca64da2a7d6c7a77abc86e6",
      "statement": "The Swift Alliance & gpi Connector (GPI-C, SYS-PNG-GPI) retrieves gpi Tracker updates in a 4-hour batch cadence (00:00, 04:00, 08:00, 12:00, 16:00, 20:00 ET) for outbound UETRs from the last 30 days and upserts them into Oracle table GPI_TRACKER_SNAPSHOT, whose only consumers are Ops Investigations Workbench and the TDIP nightly gpi_tracker_events load; there is no internal API for gpi status and the snapshot must not be exposed directly to channels.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/png-tdd-6.0-payment-network-gateway-fedwire-and-gpi-technical-design.md#L75-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1f0395eab4407be1919e76a4e6adf03a2e25c07170a4c4f314773c29a1e5de6b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e5a21b3b410e43fea3f2374e245fe769",
      "statement": "The Swift Tracker API contract permits 250,000 calls/month (renewal 2027-01-31); baseline usage from existing batch pulls plus Ops ad-hoc lookups was ~61% of quota, while estimated client-channel per-payment lookups (~2,900 outbound international wires/day with repeated views) projected to ~1.9 million calls/month, about 7x the contracted quota, which drove the recommendation that any real-time gpi design use a change-feed with internal fan-out rather than per-payment Tracker calls.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/png-tdd-6.0-payment-network-gateway-fedwire-and-gpi-technical-design.md#L90-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:418fb701c113b34af833ad1f207a2f37a37d75a14e8f2160bc6ddae8643bdf49:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_786166e1beca4aada601e0766903d857",
      "statement": "The recommendation from PNG-1544's decision was carried forward as initiative GTSI-0107 (gpi Tracker Real-Time Service / GTRS), an internal REST + event API over the Swift gpi Tracker change feed, which is not funded for 2026 with discovery planned for 2027-Q2 and build for 2027-Q3/Q4.",
